        move('the Sifrei 154:2-5 (read whole at the reading); cold_run_obey_horeb (CALL) — OH.DATA[the_law_bal_tosif][the_elder] = %s' % (OH_TOSIF['settings']['the_elder'][:60],), "'according to the law they teach you' — for words of Torah they are liable to death, not for words of the scribes (154:2); 'you shall do' — a positive commandment; 'you shall not turn' — a negative commandment (154:3-4: the pair on one act); 'RIGHT OR LEFT' — EVEN IF THEY SHOW YOU THAT RIGHT IS LEFT AND LEFT IS RIGHT, OBEY THEM (154:5); the rebellious elder liable only where the addition spoils (4:2's sealing — obey_horeb's row by CALL)")
        dat("THE WRITES sentence_binding_commanded (a STATUS) and turning_from_the_word_barred (a BLOCK) — on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DI2); the exam's person the one who follows the court's ruling against his own eyes — accepted")
        return out("do and turn not right or left (17:10-11) — the command and the prohibition on one act, right that is left, Torah not the scribes (the Sifrei 154:2-5; obey_horeb's sealing by CALL): THE WRITES sentence_binding_commanded and turning_from_the_word_barred on Israel at the chapters' own day; the one who follows the ruling against his eyes accepted", ['sentence_binding_commanded', 'turning_from_the_word_barred'])
